<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Key US Senate results: Democrats win upper chamber with victories in Texas and Iowa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12d26d8a948499082791f5a882651f65a79a461ff896422cae37b88e418ce964</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T03:52:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261104-key-us-senate-results-democrats-wrest-north-and-south-carolina-from-the-republicans" /><summary type="html">Democrats won control of the Senate in the US midterm elections Tuesday, with initial results showing the party securing shock victories in Texas, Ohio, North and South Carolina, Kansas and Iowa.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US democracy, Trump fatigue, cost of living are top issues with voters, AP survey finds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3584eaf514a4c258a8a64d153e31b1e5122a1ada3ed80f3c1f4f95ebb4757539</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T23:46:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-fatigue-cost-of-living-and-corruption-are-top-issues-with-us-voters-ap-survey-finds" /><summary type="html">Roughly 6 in 10 voters deeply disapprove of US President Donald Trump's presidency, according to an AP survey released Tuesday. About 4 in 10 say the economy is the most important issue while 3 in 10 say the state of US democracy is of primary concern – well above the number that rated crime or immigration as most important.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Historian Timothy Snyder: Trump running US foreign policy 'as though he were an organized criminal'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbbeef19747687e61029139052e021d0ce72e00e0c40f186a546e544d5b750b6</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T22:28:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261103-historian-timothy-snyder-trump-running-us-foreign-policy-as-though-he-were-an-organized-criminal" /><summary type="html">As Americans head to the polls for the midterm elections, François Picard welcomes historian Timothy Snyder, professor at the University of Toronto's Munk School of Global Affairs, for a conversation about the future of American democracy, the growing political influence of technology billionaires and the dangers of a new Gilded Age. Who really holds power in Donald Trump's America: the president or the billionaires surrounding him?</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump promised a 'Golden Age'. What has he delivered at home?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c00869811749fbc5fa30a8c105c7bf8f8d9f813e3030f3d3f69ed8621c5924bf</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:56:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261103-trump-promised-a-golden-age-what-has-he-delivered-at-home" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump promised Americans a “Golden Age” when he returned to the White House in January 2025. Since then, his administration has slashed government spending through DOGE, ramped up mass deportations, expanded ICE operations and pursued an aggressive crackdown on DEI programmes and transgender rights. But how much has he actually achieved, and at what cost? Vedika Bahl examines Trump's domestic agenda since returning to office.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Trickle or tsunami? Democrats eye gains in US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a1ded5e3b153e25252c6cc7d2d282b180ff0881c09962877ae3ce2b6e78da6a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T19:18:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261103-trickle-or-tsunami-democrats-eye-gains-in-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Will it be a trickle, a wave, or a tsunami? Election Day in the United States with Democrats hoping to take back one or both houses of Congress. We’ll track the turnout, gauge the mood and raise the curtain ahead of Midterms results that are sure to shape the last two years of Donald Trump’s second and final term. Will a US president who’s already broken norms with his maximum use of executive powers be affected by the results a little, a lot, or not at all?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Family wealth, Epstein, ‘vanity projects’: How Democrats plan to investigate Trump after midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92f1f01c96ea9592f8cf3f631f516b5def950d88e51405f0d361d4bf26e692f1</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T17:30:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-trump-family-wealth-epstein-vanity-projects-democrats-plan-to-investigate-after-midterms" /><summary type="html">Democrats are preparing to launch a flurry of investigations into President Donald Trump’s administration and business dealings if they retake one or both chambers of Congress, devising strategies to circumvent obstruction from the White House and avoid the impeachment deadlock that consumed the US legislature during Trump’s first term in office.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Texas Democrat Talarico holds last rally ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ced9f0be510b4ae82ee20ecd962e620a3e7010560a43fdedc667715c66c0e6c</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:50:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-texas-democrat-talarico-holds-last-rally-ahead-of-vote" /><summary type="html">Texas Democratic nominee James Talarico held a final rally Monday ahead of US midterm elections on November 3. His race against Republican Ken Paxton could determine which party holds a majority in the Senate. If Talarico wins, it will be the first time a Texas Senate seat's turned blue since 1988.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Over 58 million Americans cast early ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b05f9e07386ab17e97c36b118d7cc15cece4360d59c63e17f8b8a2ad246db798</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-over-58-million-americans-cast-early-ballots" /><summary type="html">How powerful is US President Donald Trump? That’s the question pollsters have been asking in the lead-up to the midterm elections. Polls have opened in dozens of US states in what is widely considered a referendum on Donald Trump. Most polls suggest Democrats will take back the House of Representatives, but could they also take the Senate and stymie Trump’s agenda during his final two years in office?</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Talarico seeks to break Democrats' 30-year losing streak in Texas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40320ffb1004aa4ed37e8485129ef15bd95ea4c0a610e9f0dc948c1d0ce850ff</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:45:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-talarico-seeks-to-break-democrats-30-year-losing-streak-in-texas" /><summary type="html">In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico is leading the polls ahead of a high-stakes US Senate race against Republican Ken Paxton. The contest is one of the most closely watched battles of the midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to end a 30-year losing streak in the state. FRANCE 24's Andrés Espinal reports from Austin, Texas.</summary></entry><entry><title>Election officials brace for possible Trump interference in the midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07fc9cb01017611d1e18ae38281668585ca00a07be4bdb4955615021c9a27951</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-how-state-officials-prepared-for-possible-trump-interference-in-the-midterms" /><summary type="html">State officials who run US elections braced for possible intervention by President Donald Trump's administration in Tuesday's midterms, fearing federal authorities loyal to the president could disrupt voting, challenge ballot counts or try to block the certification of unfavorable results.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil keeps a close eye on US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a016d07357902e44050e4c93f8cf6e4ba054b9e775022f750f5b3a3b065aa50</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:36:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-brazil-keeps-a-close-eye-on-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Brazil is keeping a close eye on the US midterm elections. Since Donald Trump's return to the White House, relations between Brasilia and Washington have grown increasingly tense. On the economic front, aggressive trade policies have subjected Brazilian imports to some of the steepest tariffs globally, exacerbating friction with the Trump administration. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Rio de Janeiro Jan Onoszko has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump focused on 'what's important to him': 'Tone-deaf for a normally shrewd populist operator'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4506d30bcd729f43135ed6b4a62304f8f6e23ec51bca55fbaa49d1979eb9c216</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T16:05:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator--19609ba997e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-focused-on-what-s-important-to-him-tone-deaf-for-a-normally-shrewd-populist-operator" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Doug Heye, Republican strategist, founder of Douglas Media, and former Communications Director for the Republican National Committee (RNC). As Americans head to the polls, Republicans face a challenge that goes beyond the familiar electoral backlash against an incumbent president. For Heye, Donald Trump's greatest political vulnerability may lie in the widening gap between his rhetoric of economic success and voters' everyday financial anxieties. "For a lot of voters, they see him focused on what's important to him, not what's important to them," Heye explains. Yet he also cautions against interpreting Democratic gains as a sign of renewed confidence in the opposition. Rather than a resurgence of partisan enthusiasm, the elections may expose an electorate increasingly disillusioned with both parties.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Michigan Senate candidate El-Sayed becomes Democrats' rising star</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb6cbc5efb9278ed70d752f15cf53901b56ed97166bec6e5e8227159bf6da666</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:41:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star--b86026836402.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-senate-candidate-el-sayed-becomes-democrats-rising-star" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, Democrat Abdul El-Sayed and Republican Mike Rogers are testing two sharply different strategies to win over voters in one of the nation's premier swing states on Tuesday, November 3, in a closely watched race that could determine control of the Senate. Progressive candidate El-Sayed has so far outpolled his Republican rival and is emerging as one of the Democratic Party's rising stars.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Michigan candidate El-Sayed pledges to tackle the affordability crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e5989f7922c513f5db0554d04e89a28e4aa9bd10cd874a33be55f7a2b4a4ed0</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:34:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis--9ec59f3a2e71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-michigan-candidate-el-sayed-pledges-to-tackle-the-affordability-crisis" /><summary type="html">The cost of living is one of the main concerns for many US voters as the midterm elections get underway. In Michigan, Democratic Senate candidate Abdul El-Sayed has pledged to "take the money out of politics and put it in your pocket", as FRANCE 24 correspondent Jessica Le Masurier reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Your donut, your vote': Texas group uses free food to attract young voters</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47e8c2bd639d5ac82eceb117691d2370a41868feed1044b5b292350f066b063b</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:26:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters--cd3ced7b6ae1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-your-donut-your-vote-texas-group-uses-free-food-to-attract-young-voters" /><summary type="html">US voters on Tuesday headed to the polls in midterm elections that could shape the political future of the country. But navigating the voting process can sometimes discourage voters – particularly younger ones. In Texas, an organisation reached out to them directly by handing out free food, to then help them overcome these obstacles. FRANCE 24's Special envoy Tarek Kai reports from Austin.</summary></entry><entry><title>Political parallels in France and the US: Anger at the ballot box and in the streets</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67d22fba36ccb6ac44faf373167eeb045da807ca967551ad7e1a4e747f438135</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:21:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets--cb3c566a3efc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261103-political-parallels-in-france-and-us-anger-at-the-ballot-box-and-in-the-streets" /><summary type="html">Anger has long been a driving force for political change, but with the midterm elections in the US and the ongoing protests in France, widespread anger in both nations is currently front and centre. We take a look at some of the common issues causing this anger on both sides of the Atlantic, including the rising cost of living, a loss of faith in institutions and an eroding of the social contract.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: All eyes on crucial Michigan Senate race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b96eb86ebc3e6b1ad1e6541710694f8270bf31b46f5bd4c84e86bc0f565ebaf</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race--7781aa8be6b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterms-all-eyes-on-crucial-michigan-senate-race" /><summary type="html">In the US midterm elections, the Senate race in Michigan has been one of the most closely watched in the country. It took an unexpected turn on Sunday after Democratic Congresswoman Haley Stevens endorsed Republican Mike Rogers over Democratic nominee Abdul El-Sayed. Both candidates made their final pitches to voters during campaign rallies on Monday evening, November 2. FRANCE 24's Jessica Le Masurier reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: A referendum on President Donald Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c584e88329e21612c4a2549780012c94a392d3f0ed1a74b83193b0f0d3caac2</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-a-referendum-on-president-donald-trump--406ec9ab4507.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-midterm-elections-a-referendum-on-president-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Americans deliver their verdict on Donald Trump's tumultuous first term in midterm elections that threaten to shatter his grip on Washington, with Democrats poised to seize the House and within striking distance of the Senate.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Supreme court rejects Trump request to set aside 20,000 California ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d508601560d3c7e59ff1a683934511818b89d6d3e7885156272fb510c62d751f</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:27:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-request-to-set-aside-20-000-california-ballots--ad9a6e802fe6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-request-to-set-aside-20-000-california-ballots" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court rejected the Trump administration’s push to force California to set aside 20,000 ballots from people the federal government claims are noncitizens, a decision that came hours before the final day of voting in the pivotal midterm elections. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>What could happen if Donald Trump loses US midterm elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:191b92641ca9206ea38698d52fde528b2928926fb0bd23488e813d6568d3b001</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-what-could-happen-if-donald-trump-loses-us-midterm-elections--9795768d7bcc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261103-what-could-happen-if-donald-trump-loses-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Americans head to the polls on Tuesday in pivotal midterm elections, with Democrats hoping to seize control of Congress and impose the first significant checks on Donald Trump's second term in the White House. But what could happen in the United States if Republicans lose control of Congress? FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US Midterms: Could a blue wave widen the centrist-progressive divide among Democrats ahead of 2028?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:31306f8ec26928fcd7d6c0c5f371172def1c047b3b2fc6628507313d9fcb292d</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T13:19:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-midterms-could-a-blue-wave-widen-the-centrist-progressive-divide-among-democrats-ahead-of-2028" /><summary type="html">As the US approaches the midterms, the contest is emerging as a referendum on Donald Trump, the resilience of American democratic institutions and the ability of a divided Democratic Party to transform widespread public dissatisfaction into a coherent political alternative. With some Republicans now seeking to distance themselves from Trump, Katy Hull, Assistant Professor of American Studies at the University of Amsterdam, suggests that the president's highly populist and personalised approach to politics is becoming an electoral liability. Philip Turle observes Republican voters turning towards the opposition "as a form of protest against Donald Trump", rather than an endorsement of the Democrats.</summary></entry><entry><title>US strikes Iran's Qeshm Island as midterm elections start</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:646670bfd2b152be82ba1522926d10978e13e530a9fc7d6966589902d7c05bdd</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T12:12:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start--40705a7ad889.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-strikes-iran-s-qeshm-island-as-midterm-elections-start" /><summary type="html">The United States has conducted defensive strikes on some Iranian targets in the Strait of Hormuz, a US official said Monday, on the eve of crucial midterm elections. The unpopular Iran war and the resulting impact on U.S. gasoline prices and other parts of the economy have been a vulnerability for Republicans as they try to keep control of Congress. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Oliver Farry has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Food stamp crisis a key campaign issue in Arizona</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6f49e1efa6c483b863bf9d7adb0cb8c9d24242782533a7f55bb34da3d9fa24f</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T11:35:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261103-us-midterm-elections-food-stamp-crisis-a-key-campaign-issue-in-arizona--615873dd3181.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261103-us-midterm-elections-food-stamp-crisis-a-key-campaign-issue-in-arizona" /><summary type="html">Arizona, a battleground state in the US midterm elections, is at the centre of a sweeping overhaul of America's social safety net. Since US President Donald Trump's tax and spending law passed last year, about half of the state's food stamp recipients have lost their benefits – the steepest drop in the country. State officials now admit that some of them are probably still eligible, but the errors have caused food insecurity to spike. The fallout has become a key issue on the campaign trail.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Midterms live: Democrats win control of House and Senate as Republican strongholds fall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6c23d00242b96e65d3f25e118f943a45c1e3c955da0e3d30d86bd8daea3c086</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T05:45:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections--73179ea277e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261103-live-americans-head-to-the-polls-to-vote-in-us-midterm-elections" /><summary type="html">Democrats have retaken control of the US House on Wednesday after flipping the Senate, delivering a decisive rebuke of Republican control of governance in Washington and ushering in a new era of congressional resistance to President Donald Trump. Democrats charted an extraordinary path to Senate victory through some of the most conservative states in the nation. Follow our liveblog for all the latest.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump promised 'no more wars'. His foreign policy tells another story</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd4026502385a2a15c103b528eb06420aafdcf66b58a7e0f0a1096cc6af416dd</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T21:34:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261102-trump-promised-no-more-wars-his-foreign-policy-tells-another-story--47a93264b68e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261102-trump-promised-no-more-wars-his-foreign-policy-tells-another-story" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump promised an "America First" foreign policy and pledged to keep the US out of foreign wars. But since returning to the White House, his administration has been deeply involved in conflicts around the world. From the war in Ukraine and threats towards Greenland and Canada, to the US intervention in Venezuela, to Trump's shifting approach to the Middle East and war with Iran, Vedika Bahl examines his foreign policy record since returning to office.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Free and fair? The midterms and the state of US democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f1cabead9b3fc3939b94850095e27d5e87b72fa0695e5d24ea2c2d50fe8dc53</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T19:37:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261102-free-and-fair-the-midterms-and-the-state-of-us-democracy--80885eec4c32.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261102-free-and-fair-the-midterms-and-the-state-of-us-democracy" /><summary type="html">How far will the president of the United States press this time if Tuesday's midterm elections don't go his party's way? From "only if the Republicans win" campaign promises to a US Justice Department that's already got involved in races, will the White House weigh on the outcome? How will ballot counting go? What's changed since Donald Trump's "stop the steal" rhetoric led to the January 6, 2021 storming of the US Capitol?</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>MAGA: Why are Trump's most loyal supporters turning against him?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0523a1c378a7cec8c39704eaee54078940aa4479a9ad7cf2afdf57e4d6a5c7db</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T19:17:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/maga-why-trump-s-most-loyal-supporters-are-turning-against-him--2635b3044ba6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/maga-why-trump-s-most-loyal-supporters-are-turning-against-him" /><summary type="html">Is Trump losing the support of the very coalition that brought him back to power?
 
Just one day before the midterm elections, Trump's approval rating stands at 32%, one of the lowest ever recorded at this stage of a presidency.
 
And discontent is growing beyond Democratic voters. Some of Trump's most loyal Republican and MAGA supporters are increasingly torn between political loyalty and economic reality. The war in Iran, rising costs linked to the Strait of Hormuz blockade, unfulfilled “America First” promises and other controversial issues, including the Epstein files scandal, are widening the rift between Trump and his electoral base.
 
Can he regain control of the diverse coalition that makes up MAGA?
 
FRANCE 24 journalist Stella Elgersma spoke to MAGA and Republican experts to explore how the movement has evolved, what its supporters want and what is driving their discontent.
 
Watch the full youtube documentary : https://youtu.be/XkehRG77itY?si=iOfIl0PwrgyX-j0X</summary></entry><entry><title>What changes if Democrats win a majority in Congress?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:524c1362aa8816da391203196574306a5faf618ca802d12121151eb4a8534d3d</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T16:29:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress--9fcfe8f120a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261102-what-changes-if-democrats-win-a-majority-in-congress" /><summary type="html">Americans head to the polls on Tuesday for the US midterm elections, which could flip the majority in one or both houses of Congress from the Republicans to the Democrats. What would a Democratic majority mean for the country's political landscape, and how might Democrats move to keep President Donald Trump in check?</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Nine dead in small plane crash near Trump's Florida home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0464ed0124497e3909c5cc7bbaddee2c48588586c6b1759785b85ea511191b5d</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:33:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home--b21dd0e6726b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261102-nine-dead-in-small-plane-crash-near-trump-s-florida-home" /><summary type="html">Nine people were killed Sunday when the Learjet they were travelling in plummeted into a neighbourhood in southern Florida, just miles from US President Donald Trump's resort home of Mar-a-Lago, officials said.</summary></entry><entry><title>Heading into the midterms, 'no US president in recent times has been as unpopular as Donald Trump'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b648e9eb8b451ebd456eb6b910cd95d1488a684d93b4026fbb61bf6500c9fe75</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:25:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/heading-into-the-midterms-no-us-president-in-recent-times-has-been-as-unpopular-as-donald-trump" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Richard Johnson, Senior Lecturer in US Politics at Queen Mary University of London. He says that "Donald Trump is damaged goods at this point in his presidency." With this uncompromising assessment, Johnson takes us through the political forces shaping the 2026 US midterm elections. Far from assuming that Trump's formidable campaigning instincts can once again mobilize Republican voters, Johnson questions whether the president's political influence has become a liability for the very party he once transformed. He points to a potentially significant realignment within the American electorate. Economic grievances, rising living costs, trade disputes and disillusionment with the war in Iran appear, in Johnson's reading, to be weakening important elements of the coalition that sustained Trump's return to power. Particularly consequential is the possibility that Latino voters, agricultural communities and sections of the MAGA electorate may be reconsidering their political loyalties or withdrawing from electoral participation altogether.</summary></entry></feed>
